Menu="Shive:2"
Title="Containers"
Tabs="true"
Markdown="false"
---
<?php require_once '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/shive/include/head.php'; ?>
<div class="shive" id="shive-containers">
  <section class="shive-card">
    <header class="shive-card-head"><h3><i class="fa fa-sort-amount-asc"></i> Start order</h3><span class="shive-hint">applies to every schedule – a dependency is a property of the containers, not of one schedule</span></header>
    <p class="shive-hint">Drag containers by their handle into the <b>sequence</b>: after a snapshot they come back up <b>top to bottom</b>, and before it they are stopped in the <b>exact reverse</b> (bottom first). Containers <b>not in the sequence</b> start before it, alphabetically. <b>Wait</b> pauses that many seconds before the next container starts, for a dependency that needs a moment to become ready; it is skipped after the last one. Keyboard: focus a row and use <kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>↑</kbd>/<kbd>↓</kbd>.</p>
    <div class="shive-order">
      <div class="shive-order-col">
        <div class="shive-col-head"><span><i class="fa fa-list-ol"></i> Sequence</span><span class="shive-hint"><i class="fa fa-arrow-down"></i> start · <i class="fa fa-arrow-up"></i> stop</span></div>
        <ol id="ctr-seq" class="shive-dnd shive-seq" data-empty="Drag containers here to give them a fixed position"><li class="shive-hint shive-loading">loading…</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div class="shive-order-col">
        <div class="shive-col-head"><span><i class="fa fa-random"></i> Not in sequence</span><span class="shive-hint">start first, A–Z</span></div>
        <ul id="ctr-pool" class="shive-dnd shive-pool" data-empty="Every container has a position"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shive-card">
    <header class="shive-card-head"><h3><i class="fa fa-database"></i> Datasets</h3><span class="shive-hint">which containers a schedule stops</span></header>
    <p class="shive-hint">Auto-discovered from each container's bind mounts (<code>docker inspect</code> → <code>findmnt -T</code> → ZFS dataset). Override where discovery cannot resolve a path (e.g. paths through <code>/mnt/user</code> that do not exist on any pool) or tick <em>ignore</em> for containers that must never be stopped.</p>
    <div class="TableContainer">
    <table class="tablesorter shift shive-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Container</th><th>Discovered datasets</th><th>Bind mounts</th><th>Override datasets (comma separated)</th><th>Ignore</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="ctr-rows"><tr><td colspan="5">loading…</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shive-savebar"><span class="buttons-spaced"><input type="button" value="Save" onclick="Shive.ctr.save()"> <input type="button" value="Rescan" onclick="Shive.ctr.load(true)"></span> <span id="ctr-msg" class="shive-hint"></span></div>
</div>
<script>$(function(){ Shive.ctr.load(false); });</script>
